{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978508-what-exactly-is-potency","id":978508,"title":"What Exactly is Potency?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-29T11:37:25-07:00","id":978508,"title":"What Exactly is Potency?","content":"Potency is something brought up quite a bit in the Mage core, but it neglects to mention how Potency is determined. I've gone over the PDF but I can't find the rules for it. Or rather, it's just unclear. Is it the successes rolled on a spellcasting check? Is it Gnosis? Please help me understand this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:55:36-07:00","id":978517,"title":"","content":"Check out page 113. Basically, Potency=dots in Arcanum, and you can take a -2 penalty on the spellcasting roll for each additional Potency you want to add. It's not related to the successes you rolled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T11:56:12-07:00","id":978518,"title":"","content":"First edition - page 118<br /> Second edition - page 113","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:07:55-07:00","id":978522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978508-what-exactly-is-potency?p=978517#post978517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out page 113. Basically, Potency=dots in Arcanum, and you can take a -2 penalty on the spellcasting roll for each additional Potency you want to add. It's not related to the successes you rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I needed to know. Thank you, you sir are a gentleman and a scholar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:12:23-07:00","id":978526,"title":"","content":"Edit: ninja's singificantly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T13:53:51-07:00","id":978600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978508-what-exactly-is-potency?p=978517#post978517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check out page 113. Basically, Potency=dots in Arcanum, and you can take a -2 penalty on the spellcasting roll for each additional Potency you want to add. It's not related to the successes you rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that some spells have Duration as the primary factor, in which case Potency=1, and you can take a -2 penalty on the spellcastinv roll for each additional Potency you want to add. Though, on such spells there is often not much use for Potency &gt; 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T14:52:31-07:00","id":978652,"title":"","content":"The biggest use of Potency &gt; 1 for Duration primary spells is to avoid them getting dispelled on you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}